		"source": "grblHAL Drivers README (github.com/grblHAL/Drivers, read 14 Nov 2026): STM32F4xx in the 'With floating point unit (FPU)' table, boards 'Blackpill / Nucleo-F411RE / Nucleo-F446RE'; Cortex-M4F single-precision FPU (DS10314 §1: Arm Cortex-M4 with FPU)"
	},
	"sources": [
		"ST STM32_open_pin_data mcu/STM32F411C(C-E)Ux.xml (BSD-3-Clause)",
		"DS10314 Rev 8 (Jan 2024): power supply scheme (VDD n × 100 nF + 4.7 µF; VDDA 100 nF + 1 µF, here 100 nF), Table 16 VCAP_1 4.7 µF ESR < 1 Ω with a single VCAP pin, Fig. 'NRST' 0.1 µF, boot modes (BOOT0 low: flash)",
		"No crystal: STM32duino's generic F411CE clock (variants/STM32F4xx/F411C(C-E)(U-Y)/generic_clock.c) runs from the HSI; the Black Pill's variant needs its 25 MHz HSE. USB OTG FS needs the HSE (HSI ±1% is outside USB's tolerance), so the profile has no usb and the board doesn't wire it",
		"Console USART1 on PA9/PA10: the pins ST's ROM bootloader also listens on (AN2606)"
	],
